/**
\addtogroup dense

The functions of `laplace::dense` are not header-only and are not `LAPLACE_HD`.
They run on the host only, take Kokkos Views that the host can read, and do their work with Eigen in a static library, `laplace_dense` (CMake target `Laplace::dense`), which a program that uses them must link.

## Overview

This module provides dense matrix decompositions, linear system solves, spectral problems, and null space computations on the host:
- \ref laplace::dense::cholesky_decomposition "cholesky_decomposition()": Cholesky factorization of a symmetric positive definite matrix.
- \ref laplace::dense::triangular_solve "triangular_solve()": in-place triangular system solve \f$\operatorname{op}(T) X = B\f$.
- \ref laplace::dense::pivoted_qr_decomposition "pivoted_qr_decomposition()": column-pivoted QR decomposition \f$A P = Q R\f$.
- \ref laplace::dense::svd_decomposition "svd_decomposition()": singular value decomposition \f$A = U \operatorname{diag}(s) V^\top\f$.
- \ref laplace::dense::symmetric_eigen_decomposition "symmetric_eigen_decomposition()": spectral decomposition of a real symmetric matrix \f$A = V \operatorname{diag}(w) V^\top\f$.
- \ref laplace::dense::generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition "generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition()": generalized symmetric-definite eigenvalue problem \f$A V = B V \operatorname{diag}(w)\f$ with \f$V^\top B V = I\f$.
- \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis()": orthonormal basis \f$T\f$ of the null space of a matrix \f$C\f$ (\f$C T = 0\f$, \f$T^\top T = I\f$).

The status types and option enums:
- \ref laplace::dense::dense_decomposition_status "dense_decomposition_status": status struct containing success indicator, numerical rank, and failure reason.
- \ref laplace::dense::dense_failure "dense_failure": failure codes for numerical conditions.
- \ref laplace::dense::dense_triangle "dense_triangle": selector for lower or upper triangular storage.
- \ref laplace::dense::dense_operation "dense_operation": selector for identity or transpose operations.

## Conventions

### Views and memory layout

Matrices are passed as rank-2 Kokkos Views of \c double with column-major storage layout (`Kokkos::LayoutLeft`), residing in a memory space accessible from the host (such as `Kokkos::HostSpace`).
A View in device memory (such as `Kokkos::CudaSpace`) is rejected at compile time by a static assertion.
Vectors are passed as rank-1 Kokkos Views of \c double, and the permutation vector `perm` is passed as a rank-1 Kokkos View of \c int.
Output Views must not have a const value type.

### Symmetric matrices and triangular storage

For symmetric inputs (\f$A\f$ in \ref laplace::dense::cholesky_decomposition "cholesky_decomposition()", \ref laplace::dense::symmetric_eigen_decomposition "symmetric_eigen_decomposition()", and \ref laplace::dense::generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition "generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition()", and \f$B\f$ in \ref laplace::dense::generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition "generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition()"), only the lower triangle is read.
The strictly upper triangle is not read; a NaN or an infinity located in the upper triangle is not seen and does not affect the calculation.

### Status reporting and exceptions

Every decomposition function returns a \ref laplace::dense::dense_decomposition_status "dense_decomposition_status" struct with fields:
- `success`: boolean indicating whether the decomposition succeeded.
- `rank`: numerical rank for \ref laplace::dense::pivoted_qr_decomposition "pivoted_qr_decomposition()", \ref laplace::dense::svd_decomposition "svd_decomposition()", and \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis()", or dimension \f$n\f$ otherwise.
- `reason`: a \ref laplace::dense::dense_failure "dense_failure" code indicating the cause when `success` is \c false.

Numerical outcomes are reported through the status struct and are never thrown as exceptions:
- `dense_failure::not_positive_definite`: \f$A\f$ in Cholesky decomposition, or \f$B\f$ in the generalized problem, is not positive definite.
- `dense_failure::singular`: a diagonal entry of the triangular matrix \f$T\f$ is zero during a triangular solve.
- `dense_failure::no_convergence`: an iterative SVD or eigensolver failed to converge.
- `dense_failure::non_finite_input`: a NaN or an infinity was encountered among the entries read.

A low numerical rank is not a failure; it is reported in the `rank` field.
When `success` is \c false, the outputs are unspecified.
Invalid dimensions or incompatible View shapes throw `std::invalid_argument`.

### Rank determination

The numerical rank \f$r\f$ counts the singular values \f$s_i\f$ satisfying
\f[
s_i > \text{tol} \cdot s_1
\f]
for \ref laplace::dense::svd_decomposition "svd_decomposition()" and \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis()" (with \f$s_1\f$ the largest singular value), or the diagonal entries of \f$R\f$ satisfying
\f[
|R_{kk}| > \text{tol} \cdot |R_{11}|
\f]
for \ref laplace::dense::pivoted_qr_decomposition "pivoted_qr_decomposition()".
By default, the relative tolerance is
\f[
\text{tol} = \max(m, n)\,\varepsilon
\f]
where \f$m\f$ is the row count, \f$n\f$ is the column count, and \f$\varepsilon = 2^{-52}\f$ is machine precision of double precision, matching the rank rule of NumPy's `matrix_rank` and MATLAB's `rank`.
When the caller provides a non-negative `relative_tolerance`, that value is used as \f$\text{tol}\f$.
The null space computation in \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis()" uses the singular value decomposition.

### Output shapes

For an \f$m \times n\f$ matrix with \f$p = \min(m, n)\f$, thin or full factorizations are selected by the shapes of the output Views:
- In \ref laplace::dense::pivoted_qr_decomposition "pivoted_qr_decomposition()", \f$Q\f$ may be \f$m \times p\f$ (thin) or \f$m \times m\f$ (full); \f$R\f$ must have shape \f$p \times n\f$ when \f$Q\f$ is thin, or \f$m \times n\f$ when \f$Q\f$ is full.
- In \ref laplace::dense::svd_decomposition "svd_decomposition()", \f$U\f$ may be \f$m \times p\f$ (thin) or \f$m \times m\f$ (full), and \f$V\f$ may be \f$n \times p\f$ (thin) or \f$n \times n\f$ (full), chosen independently. Singular values \f$s\f$ always have length \f$p\f$.
- In \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis()", \f$T\f$ is reallocated to shape \f$n \times (n - r)\f$, where \f$r\f$ is the numerical rank of \f$C\f$. The output View \f$T\f$ must be a managed View. When \f$m = 0\f$, \f$T\f$ is the \f$n \times n\f$ identity matrix and \f$r = 0\f$.

### Threading

One thread per call; several decompositions in parallel are the caller's to arrange.

## Decompositions

### Cholesky decomposition

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::cholesky_decomposition "cholesky_decomposition(A, L)":
\f[
A = L L^\top
\f]
where \f$A\f$ is \f$n \times n\f$ symmetric positive definite and \f$L\f$ is \f$n \times n\f$ lower triangular.
The strictly upper triangular part of \f$L\f$ is set to zero.
If \f$A\f$ is not positive definite, returns `dense_failure::not_positive_definite`.

### Triangular solve

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::triangular_solve "triangular_solve(T, B, triangle, operation)":
\f[
\operatorname{op}(T) X = B
\f]
solved in place on \f$B\f$ (\f$n \times k\f$), with \f$T\f$ (\f$n \times n\f$) lower or upper triangular.
\f$\operatorname{op}(T)\f$ is \f$T\f$ when `operation` is `dense_operation::identity`, and \f$T^\top\f$ when `operation` is `dense_operation::transpose`.
If any diagonal entry of \f$T\f$ is zero, returns `dense_failure::singular`.

### Pivoted QR decomposition

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::pivoted_qr_decomposition "pivoted_qr_decomposition(A, Q, R, perm, relative_tolerance)":
\f[
A P = Q R
\f]
where \f$A\f$ is \f$m \times n\f$, \f$Q\f$ has orthonormal columns, and \f$R\f$ is upper triangular.
Column \f$j\f$ of \f$Q R\f$ equals column \f$\operatorname{perm}[j]\f$ of \f$A\f$.
The numerical rank of \f$A\f$ is returned in the status.

### Singular value decomposition

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::svd_decomposition "svd_decomposition(A, U, s, V, relative_tolerance)":
\f[
A = U \operatorname{diag}(s) V^\top
\f]
where \f$s\f$ has \f$p = \min(m, n)\f$ singular values in decreasing order \f$s_1 \ge s_2 \ge \dots \ge s_p \ge 0\f$, and \f$U\f$ and \f$V\f$ have orthonormal columns.
The numerical rank of \f$A\f$ is returned in the status.

### Symmetric eigendecomposition

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::symmetric_eigen_decomposition "symmetric_eigen_decomposition(A, w, V)":
\f[
A = V \operatorname{diag}(w) V^\top
\f]
for symmetric \f$A\f$ (\f$n \times n\f$), where eigenvalues \f$w\f$ are in increasing order \f$w_1 \le w_2 \le \dots \le w_n\f$ and \f$V\f$ is orthogonal (\f$V^\top V = I\f$).

### Generalized symmetric eigendecomposition

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition "generalized_symmetric_eigen_decomposition(A, B, w, V)":
\f[
A V = B V \operatorname{diag}(w) \quad \text{with} \quad V^\top B V = I
\f]
for symmetric \f$A\f$ and symmetric positive definite \f$B\f$ (\f$n \times n\f$), with eigenvalues \f$w\f$ in increasing order.
If \f$B\f$ is not positive definite, returns `dense_failure::not_positive_definite`.

### Null space basis

Evaluated by \ref laplace::dense::null_space_basis "null_space_basis(C, T, relative_tolerance)":
\f[
C T = 0 \quad \text{with} \quad T^\top T = I
\f]
providing an orthonormal basis \f$T\f$ of the null space of \f$C\f$ (\f$m \times n\f$).
The output View \f$T\f$ is reallocated to \f$n \times (n - r)\f$, with \f$r\f$ the rank of \f$C\f$ computed via SVD.

## Reduction of the generalized problem

The generalized symmetric eigenvalue problem \f$A V = B V \operatorname{diag}(w)\f$ with \f$V^\top B V = I\f$ is reduced to a standard symmetric eigenvalue problem with the Cholesky factor \f$L\f$ of \f$B\f$ (\f$B = L L^\top\f$):
1. Compute the Cholesky factorization \f$B = L L^\top\f$.
2. Form \f$\tilde{A} = L^{-1} A L^{-\top}\f$.
3. Compute the standard symmetric eigendecomposition \f$\tilde{A} Y = Y \operatorname{diag}(w)\f$.
4. Compute \f$V = L^{-\top} Y\f$, so that \f$V^\top B V = Y^\top L^{-1} B L^{-\top} Y = Y^\top Y = I\f$.

The reduction with the Cholesky factor of \f$B\f$ is not backward stable when \f$B\f$ is ill-conditioned: its error on an eigenvalue near zero is of the order of \f$\varepsilon \|A\| \|B^{-1}\|\f$ (the error of eigenvalues near zero grows with the condition of \f$B\f$).

## Accuracy

The general method of accuracy verification is described on the page \ref accuracy "How accuracy is measured".
Reference values for `laplace::dense` were generated by `tools/reference/dense.py` using mpmath at 200 bits on 17 test cases: matrices built from chosen spectra and random orthogonal factors at 200 bits, then rounded to double precision.
The reference values are the eigenvalues or singular values of the rounded double-precision matrices, computed in mpmath at 200 bits.

### Error measures

Error measures are defined in `benchmarks/dense_cases.hpp` and evaluated in units of machine precision \f$\varepsilon = 2^{-52}\f$:
- **Eigenvalues and singular values.** For symmetric and rectangular matrices, the error of computed values \f$v\f$ against reference values \f$v_{\text{ref}}\f$ is measured in units of \f$\varepsilon\f$ times the largest reference value:
  \f[
  \frac{\max_i |v_i - v_{i,\text{ref}}|}{\varepsilon \max_i |v_{i,\text{ref}}|}
  \f]
- **Generalized eigenvalues.** For the generalized problem, the error of each eigenvalue \f$w_i\f$ is scaled by its condition number \f$\kappa_i\f$:
  \f[
  \frac{|w_i - w_{i,\text{ref}}|}{\varepsilon \kappa_i}, \quad \kappa_i = (\|A\|_F + |w_i| \|B\|_F) \|v_i\|_2^2
  \f]
  where \f$v_i\f$ is the \f$i\f$-th column of \f$V\f$ (\f$B\f$-normalized, so \f$v_i^\top B v_i = 1\f$).
- **Residuals and loss of orthonormality.** All residuals and departures from orthonormality are measured using the Frobenius norm \f$\|\cdot\|_F\f$ in units of \f$\varepsilon\f$:
  - Symmetric eigenproblem residual: \f$\|A V - V \operatorname{diag}(w)\|_F / (\|A\|_F \varepsilon)\f$.
  - Symmetric eigenvector orthonormality: \f$\|V^\top V - I\|_F / \varepsilon\f$.
  - Cholesky decomposition residual: \f$\|L L^\top - A\|_F / (\|A\|_F \varepsilon)\f$.
  - Triangular solve residual: \f$\|\operatorname{op}(T) X - B\|_F / (\|T\|_F \|X\|_F \varepsilon)\f$, with \f$T\f$ the Cholesky factor of a positive definite case (or its transpose for the upper triangle) and the right-hand sides \f$B\f$ the matrix \f$A\f$ of that case, evaluated over all four combinations of triangle and operation.
  - Generalized eigenproblem residual: \f$\|A V - B V \operatorname{diag}(w)\|_F / ((\|A\|_F + \|B\|_F \max_i |w_i|) \|V\|_F \varepsilon)\f$.
  - Generalized orthonormality: \f$\|V^\top B V - I\|_F / (\|V\|_F^2 \|B\|_F \varepsilon)\f$.
  - SVD reconstruction residual: \f$\|U_p \operatorname{diag}(s) V_p^\top - A\|_F / (\|A\|_F \varepsilon)\f$, where \f$p = \min(m, n)\f$ and \f$U_p, V_p\f$ are the first \f$p\f$ columns.
  - SVD orthonormality: \f$\max(\|U^\top U - I\|_F, \|V^\top V - I\|_F) / \varepsilon\f$.
  - Pivoted QR residual: \f$\|Q R - A P\|_F / (\|A\|_F \varepsilon)\f$, where column \f$j\f$ of \f$A P\f$ is column \f$\operatorname{perm}[j]\f$ of \f$A\f$.
  - Pivoted QR orthonormality: \f$\|Q^\top Q - I\|_F / \varepsilon\f$.
  - Null space constraint residual: \f$\|C T\|_F / (\|C\|_F \varepsilon)\f$.
  - Null space basis orthonormality: \f$\|T^\top T - I\|_F / \varepsilon\f$.

### Symmetric matrices

Evaluated on 6 test cases (the Cholesky factor and the triangular solve on the four positive definite ones) with dimensions \f$n \in \{5, \dots, 60\}\f$, including positive definite matrices, an indefinite matrix, a matrix with condition number \f$10^{12}\f$, a matrix with a cluster of ten eigenvalues within \f$9 \times 10^{-9}\f$, and a semidefinite matrix with four zero eigenvalues:

| Quantity | Measured error (gcc) | Measured error (CUDA) | Test bound |
|---|---|---|---|
| Eigenvalues \f$w\f$ | 12.2 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 12.2 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 19 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Residual \f$\|A V - V \operatorname{diag}(w)\|_F\f$ | 9.85 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 9.92 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 15 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Orthonormality \f$\|V^\top V - I\|_F\f$ | 71.0 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 72.2 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 110 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Cholesky residual \f$\|L L^\top - A\|_F\f$ | 0.56 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.62 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 1 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Triangular solve residual \f$\|\operatorname{op}(T) X - B\|_F\f$ | 0.33 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.44 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 1 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |

The maximum orthonormality error of 72.2 \f$\varepsilon\f$ occurs at \f$n = 60\f$.
Test bounds in automated regression tests (`tests/dense/test_dense.cpp`) are set to about 1.5 times the larger of the measured errors on gcc and CUDA.

### Generalized symmetric pairs

Evaluated on 3 test cases with dimensions \f$n \in \{5, 20, 40\}\f$, with condition numbers of \f$B\f$ equal to \f$10^2\f$, \f$10^6\f$, and \f$10^3\f$:

| Quantity | Measured error (gcc) | Measured error (CUDA) | Test bound |
|---|---|---|---|
| Eigenvalues \f$w\f$ | 1270.3 \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i\f$ | 1270.3 \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i\f$ | 1910 \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i\f$ |
| Residual \f$\|A V - B V \operatorname{diag}(w)\|_F\f$ | 0.16 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.19 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.3 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Orthonormality \f$\|V^\top B V - I\|_F\f$ | 0.07 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.10 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 0.15 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |

In the generalized problem with condition number of \f$B\f$ equal to \f$10^6\f$ (case 8, where \f$A\f$ is a second-difference penalty of rank \f$n - 2\f$), the error reaches 1270.3 \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i\f$ at the two zero eigenvalues (absolute error \f$3.6 \times 10^{-10}\f$ against \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i = 4 \times 10^{-14}\f$), reflecting the condition limit of the Cholesky reduction.
For the other cases (condition of \f$B\f$ equal to \f$10^2\f$ and \f$10^3\f$), the error is within 1.4 \f$\varepsilon \kappa_i\f$.

### Rectangular matrices

Evaluated on 8 test cases with shapes from \f$1 \times 20\f$ to \f$40 \times 25\f$, with expected ranks 5, 5, 18, 10, 30, 1, 3 and 2 (three of them below \f$\min(m, n)\f$, and the \f$30 \times 30\f$ case of full rank with condition \f$10^{12}\f$), among them a single row of ones and three rows of integers whose third row is the sum of the other two:

| Quantity | Measured error (gcc) | Measured error (CUDA) | Test bound |
|---|---|---|---|
| Singular values \f$s\f$ | 7.93 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 7.93 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 12 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| SVD residual \f$\|U_p \operatorname{diag}(s) V_p^\top - A\|_F\f$ | 14.38 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 14.39 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 22 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| SVD orthonormality \f$\max(\|U^\top U - I\|_F, \|V^\top V - I\|_F)\f$ | 44.17 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 44.53 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 67 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Pivoted QR residual \f$\|Q R - A P\|_F\f$ | 1.55 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 1.56 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 2.4 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Pivoted QR orthonormality \f$\|Q^\top Q - I\|_F\f$ | 12.33 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 14.12 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 22 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Null space residual \f$\|C T\|_F\f$ | 0.94 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 1.74 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 2.7 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |
| Null space orthonormality \f$\|T^\top T - I\|_F\f$ | 12.09 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 13.07 \f$\varepsilon\f$ | 20 \f$\varepsilon\f$ |

The SVD and pivoted QR ranks matched the expected ranks across all eight cases, and the number of null-space basis columns matched \f$n - r\f$ exactly in all cases with \f$m < n\f$.

## Execution times

Timings measured in `benchmarks/dense.cpp` on one gcc thread, in milliseconds (ms) per call, across matrix dimensions \f$K \in \{20, 50, 200, 1000\}\f$:

| \f$K\f$ | Cholesky | Triangular solve | Pivoted QR | SVD | Symmetric eigen | Generalized eigen | Null space (\f$3 \times K\f$) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 20 | 0.0008 ms | 0.0012 ms | 0.0063 ms | 0.055 ms | 0.011 ms | 0.016 ms | 0.0026 ms |
| 50 | 0.0066 ms | 0.011 ms | 0.053 ms | 0.50 ms | 0.088 ms | 0.14 ms | 0.0059 ms |
| 200 | 0.16 ms | 0.52 ms | 2.18 ms | 10.4 ms | 5.97 ms | 6.53 ms | 0.070 ms |
| 1000 | 15.6 ms | 44.3 ms | 194 ms | 608 ms | 459 ms | 736 ms | 3.3 ms |

Triangular solve was measured with \f$K\f$ right-hand sides.
Pivoted QR includes the formation of \f$Q\f$, and SVD includes the formation of \f$U\f$ and \f$V\f$.

## Example

The following example computes an orthonormal basis for the null space of a \f$2 \times 4\f$ matrix of constraints:

```cpp
constexpr int m = 2;
constexpr int n = 4;
Kokkos::View<double**, Kokkos::LayoutLeft, Kokkos::HostSpace> C("C", m, n);

// Constraint 1: sum to zero
C(0, 0) = 1.0;
C(0, 1) = 1.0;
C(0, 2) = 1.0;
C(0, 3) = 1.0;

// Constraint 2: linear contrast
C(1, 0) = -3.0;
C(1, 1) = -1.0;
C(1, 2) = 1.0;
C(1, 3) = 3.0;

// Output View T is reallocated to n x (n - rank)
Kokkos::View<double**, Kokkos::LayoutLeft, Kokkos::HostSpace> T("T", 1, 1);
const laplace::dense::dense_decomposition_status status =
    laplace::dense::null_space_basis(C, T);

if (status.success) {
  // status.rank is 2; T has shape 4 x 2 and satisfies C * T = 0 and T^T * T = I
  const int null_dim = n - status.rank;
  // Columns of T provide the orthonormal null space basis
} else {
  // Handle numerical failure reported in status.reason
}
```

## References

- Eigen: a C++ template library for linear algebra, version 3.4, https://eigen.tuxfamily.org, Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL2).
- mpmath: cited under \ref accuracy "How accuracy is measured".

*/
